/* NOTE ( pImmig, EN )
** Updated on 25-Nov-2020 by Joel (https://f3eaipitcap01.statcan.ca/MicroSim/POHEM/merge_requests/9. The previous update did not account for emmigrant data when computing immigrant counts.
** Updated on 28-Sep-2020 by Joel (https://f3eaipitcap01.statcan.ca/MicroSim/POHEM/merge_requests/8).
** Updated SEP 2015 by Claude:  NS and NB were mixed up for years 2001 to 2013 inclusively  (all ages, all sexes)**
** Updated JAN 2015 from CANSIM up to 2013 and the offical population projections to 2100- Deirdre Hennessy see H:\POHEM\Parameters\Immig **
>As with the pPopulation we changed the dimensions of this parameter begining in 1971 to begin in 2001.
>For years 2001-2013, we used observed estimates from CANSIM for ages up to 99. 
For age group 100+ we had no data, therefore there are zeros for every year of age up to 119.
Data Source: CANSIM table 051-0001, Statistics Canada. Obtained November 21, 2014.

>For years 2014-2100, used official population projections from the cohort component model for ages 0-110 
These were the medium term projections M3 (From the demography documentation: The medium-growth and 1999/2000 to 2002/2003 interprovincial 
migrations trends scenario is defined by the following assumptions: a Canadian total fertility rate that reaches 
1.67 births per woman in 2021/2022 and remains constant thereafter; a Canadian life expectancy that reaches 87.5 years 
for males and 89.1 years for females in 2062/2063; interprovincial migration based on the trends observed between 1999/2000 
and 2002/2003; a national immigration rate that reaches 0.75% in 2022/2023 and remains constant thereafter; 
an annual number of non-permanent residents (Canada) that reaches 864,600 in 2021 and remains constant thereafter; 
a national net emigration rate of 0.19%.). 
For ages 110-119 no data was available these cells were zeroed
>Data Source: Demography Division, Statistics Canada. Obtained from Simone Coulomb in November 2014
** Updated Jan 25, 2007 from CANSIM ** 
Immigrants, Canada by sex and years 1971-2005 and single age except 90+ 
The 90+ age group was set to 0.
Projections after year 2005 were not available from CANSIM, so counts are  
set at 2005 levels. 
CANSIM Table 051-0011 - International migrants, by age group and sex, Canada, provinces, and territories, annual (Persons)(1) 
Survey or program details: Estimates of Population by Age and Sex for Canada, the Provinces and the Territories - 3604 
Local file: J:\MODELING\Population and Demography\CANSIM0051-0011 Immig 1971-2005 (Saved May 25, 2007) 
*/ 

	 //EN Number of new immigrants by sex, age, province and year
